Hi,
I read tree-data book and found that there is a fantastic combination of phylogenetic tree and other data. I wonder whether there is a parameter that can control the ratio between left and right panel. Presently, it is in equally split.
library(ggridges)
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-2>
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-3>data("GlobalPatterns")
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-4>GP <- GlobalPatterns
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-5>GP <- prune_taxa(taxa_sums(GP) > 600, GP)
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-6>sample_data(GP)$human <- get_variable(GP, "SampleType") %in%
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-7>  c("Feces", "Skin")
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-8>
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-9>mergedGP <- merge_samples(GP, "SampleType")
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-10>mergedGP <- rarefy_even_depth(mergedGP,rngseed=394582)
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-11>mergedGP <- tax_glom(mergedGP,"Order")
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-12>
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-13>melt_simple <- psmelt(mergedGP) %>%
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-14>  filter(Abundance < 120) %>%
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-15>  select(OTU, val=Abundance)
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-16>
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-17>ggtree(mergedGP) +
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-18>  geom_tippoint(aes(color=Phylum), size=1.5) +
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-19>  geom_facet(mapping = aes(x=val,group=label,
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-20>                           fill=Phylum),
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-21>            data = melt_simple,
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-22>            geom = geom_density_ridges,
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-23>            panel="Abundance",
 <https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter10.html#cb215-24>            color='grey80', lwd=.3)

